WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.180
- [Narrator] This surreal fortress

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.970
was built on the remains
of a medieval castle

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.253
by one very curious man.

00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:12.325
(inquisitive music)

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.860
Rocchetta Mattei is located

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.823
in the Northern Alpines of Italy.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.960
Construction began in 1850

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.490
and was commissioned
by Count Cesare Mattei,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.253
who was a self-taught inventor
and quite the eccentric.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.480
His intention was for this castle

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.980
to be the home of his medical revolution,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.750
a concept based on using
the energy of plants

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.523
to heal physical ailments.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.140
His eclectic sensibilities

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.070
are reflected in the labyrinth design

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.420
of randomly connected rooms.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.580
Mattei passed away at 87 years
old, but he didn't go far.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.840
He's buried in the chapel,
which is decorated elaborately

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.393
as a replication of
Cordoba's Mezquita in Spain.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.690
For the last 20 years of his
life, he never left the castle;

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.350
and after his death, it was
all but abandoned until 2005,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.740
when an independent group took
over and restored the site,

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.180
opening it back up for
the public to explore

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.673
this very unusual residence.

00:01:22.537 --> 00:01:24.704
(chiming)

